LAST_SUCCESS=Task 21 verified OK — 440 Hz beep heard on Pixel 2 XL speaker at app launch. Full Path B-AAudio pipeline working end-to-end via media.aaudio + rsbinder.
NOTES=B5 surfaced 4 issues, all fixed: (1) AAUDIO_SHARING_MODE constants were swapped (EXCLUSIVE=0/SHARED=1 not alphabetical); (2) needed BnAAudioClient stub via registerClient before openStream — service requires a registered client for SHARED dispatch; (3) Pixel 2 XL HAL only MMAPs stereo, so WIT/test had to use STEREO channel layout; (4) writeCounter/data ring fds come from AAudio marked writeable=false but MUST be mmap'd PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE (AOSP libaaudio ignores that flag) — A2 honored it strictly causing SEGV_ACCERR, fixed by hard-coding /*writeable=*/true at the AAudio call site; (5) standard AAudio order is write-then-start, not start-then-write — calling start first lets the HAL mixer race the producer and skew readCounter. Scripts/build-apk.sh + scripts/env-android.sh added for reusable APK builds. AttributionSourceState left as the empty stub — full-shape attempt regressed to BadType (recursive Vec<Box<Self>> in `next` field unsupported by rsbinder-aidl 0.7.0).
